faqs:
  - q: How does local SEO help contractors get more jobs?
    a: When homeowners need a contractor, they search Google for things like kitchen remodel near me or general contractor plus their city. Local SEO makes sure your business shows up in those search results. We build service pages, location pages, and optimize your Google Business Profile so you appear when customers are actively looking for what you do. Our D One Builders client went from invisible online to capturing over 3,000 monthly searches.
  - q: How do I get more reviews for my contracting business?
    a: We set up automated review request systems that send a text or email to clients after a job is complete. The message includes a direct link to your Google Business Profile, making it easy for happy customers to leave a review with just a few taps. More reviews means better local rankings and more trust from potential customers.
  - q: Can customers request quotes directly through my website?
    a: Yes. We build custom lead capture forms that collect exactly the information you need including project type, timeline, budget range, and photos. Every submission goes directly into your CRM with automatic notifications so you can respond quickly. We also set up automated follow-up sequences so no lead falls through the cracks.
  - q: How long does it take to see results from SEO?
    a: Most contractors start seeing measurable improvements in search rankings within 60 to 90 days. Significant traffic growth typically happens within 3 to 6 months. SEO is a compounding investment. The content and optimizations we build today keep working for you months and years from now, unlike paid ads that stop the moment you stop paying.
  - q: Do I really need a website? Most of my work comes from referrals.
    a: Referrals are great, but even referred customers will Google you before calling. If they find a dated website or no website at all, you lose credibility. A professional site with project photos, reviews, and clear service descriptions validates the referral and makes it easy for them to contact you. Plus, a good website captures the customers who do not have a referral and are searching online.
